1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,946
icm-architect turns a way of working into a folder an agent can run.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,251
It goes in two directions: it builds a workspace from

3
00:00:10,251 --> 00:00:13,687
what you describe, or restructures one you already have.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,354
A cold agent opens the root file.

5
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:23,420
Eighteen lines: what this is, and where the method lives.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,150
The method asks one question first: what is the repeating unit of work?

7
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,616
The answer picks one of six forms.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,754
Every working folder gets a contract: what it reads, what

9
00:00:44,754 --> 00:00:48,047
it does, what it writes, and what a person checks.

10
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,831
New work begins by copying one of eight blank starters.

11
00:00:56,831 --> 00:00:59,339
That is the method's own tenth rule.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,613
One test decides any of it: an agent with no memory

13
00:01:08,613 --> 00:01:12,581
must orient, act and report status from the files alone.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,225
Two road signs.

15
00:01:16,225 --> 00:01:20,964
Two files here are called CLAUDE.md, only one is the door.

16
00:01:20,964 --> 00:01:23,905
And finished work is kept elsewhere.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,324
Open the catalog, then one card.

18
00:01:27,324 --> 00:01:28,994
That is the whole rule.
